# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working
# tree to CRLF. The structural tests assert source text with "\n", so a CRLF
# checkout fails them even though the committed blobs are LF. Declaring the
# attribute makes checkouts platform-independent (attributes win over
# core.autocrlf), and `text=auto` keeps real binaries untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
